# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Loaded by dotenvy in development (and sourced by
# `nix run .#invest-core`). Topology DEFAULTS live in flake.nix (`ports`); anything set
# here or in the environment wins. Normally this file holds per-machine overrides only.
RUST_LOG=info,invest_core=debug

# ── Control plane ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@localhost:5432/invest
# GRPC_ADDR=127.0.0.1:50071
# DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS=10
# RELAY_DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS=3

# ── Unit ledger: invest's OWN TigerBeetle cluster (never banking's :3033) ─────
# TIGERBEETLE_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:3034
# TIGERBEETLE_CLUSTER_ID=0

# ── Inbound auth: access tokens of concierge's `invest` relying party ─────────
# Verified locally against concierge's JWKS, fetched over its gRPC.
# AUTH_ISSUER=https://auth.concierge.ev
# AUTH_AUDIENCE=invest
# AUTH_JWKS_GRPC_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:55670

# ── Money: banking's scope ledger (scope.v1.ScopeLedgerService) ──────────────
# The client side of banking's SCOPE_LEDGER_* listener (banking piggybank/core/.env.example).
# Unset SCOPE_LEDGER_ADDR ⇒ no money ledger: the reserved allocations' NAV answers
# UNAVAILABLE. Once it is set, every variable below is required and checked at boot.
# SCOPE_LEDGER_ADDR=https://127.0.0.1:50054
# The CA banking's listener certificate chains to — pinned, not the public roots.
# SCOPE_LEDGER_TLS_CA_PEM_FILE=
# invest's client certificate + key; banking maps the certificate's SHA-256 to `invest`.
# SCOPE_LEDGER_TLS_CERT_PEM_FILE=
# SCOPE_LEDGER_TLS_KEY_PEM_FILE=
# The name banking's certificate carries, when it is not the host of SCOPE_LEDGER_ADDR.
# SCOPE_LEDGER_TLS_DOMAIN=
# A `typ=service` token with `sub = invest`, until banking's MintServiceToken lands.
# SCOPE_LEDGER_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# ── People: concierge's lifecycle and scope streams → the `users` projection ──
# The same address and credential publish invest's permission catalog at boot.
# Unset CONCIERGE_GRPC_ADDR ⇒ the projection does not run and the catalog is not published:
# nobody is known to invest, every permission check and every mint is refused. Set ⇒
# CONCIERGE_CLIENT_SECRET is required.
# CONCIERGE_GRPC_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:55670
# CONCIERGE_CLIENT_ID=invest
# The secret concierge holds as RP_CLIENT_SECRET_INVEST (concierge .env.example).
# CONCIERGE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# For concierge's TLS listener (https://…:55672): its CA, required, and the certificate's
# name when it is not the address's host.
# CONCIERGE_TLS_CA_PEM_FILE=
# CONCIERGE_TLS_DOMAIN=

# ── Observability ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required in production (the boot fails without it); a silent no-op when unset elsewhere.
# SENTRY_DSN=
APP_ENV=development
